You want to install RabbitMQ 3.13.6 with Erlang 26.2 on Ubuntu 26.04.

The important point is to install compatible, pinned versions rather than Ubuntu's default packages, which may provide newer versions.

We'll set up RabbitMQ as a background service so you can manage it from the terminal and, optionally, through its web-based management GUI.

## Recommended method: Docker on Ubuntu 26.04

RabbitMQ 3.13.6 supports Erlang/OTP 26.0 through 26.2.x, so your requested versions are compatible.

