Docker is a convenient way to run this older RabbitMQ version on Ubuntu 26.04 without changing your system's Erlang installation.

### 1. Install Docker

bash
```
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y docker.io
sudo systemctl enable --now docker
```

### 2. Start RabbitMQ 3.13.6 with the management GUI

bash
```
sudo docker run -d \
  --name rabbitmq \
  --restart unless-stopped \
  -p 5672:5672 \
  -p 15672:15672 \
  rabbitmq:3.13.6-management
```

This uses the official RabbitMQ image with the management plugin.

